    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RSS to Instagram with AI\n\nTurn RSS news into an Instagram post with AI-written copy and a generated image. The workflow selects up to three articles, emails the draft, hosts the visual on Cloudinary, and publishes through Meta's Graph API.\n\n## How it works\n- Read an RSS feed and select up to three relevant articles.\n- Write the Instagram copy and email the draft.\n- Generate an image, add text overlays and host it on Cloudinary.\n- Create the Instagram media container, check readiness, publish and verify.\n\n## Setup\n- Install the Cloudinary node and connect OpenAI, Gmail, Drive, Cloudinary and Meta credentials.\n- Replace feed, email, folder, Cloudinary and Instagram account settings.\n- Check the AI prompts, image settings and Meta publishing permissions.\n- Test with your own accounts, review the result, then enable the schedule.\n\n## Customize\n- Choose your RSS feed, topics and publishing schedule.\n- Adjust the selection prompt, writing style and image overlays.\n- Set the email recipient, storage folder and Instagram account.\n\n## Additional info\n- The draft email is a notification, not an approval gate.\n- Uses the Cloudinary community node; provider charges may apply.\n- [Setup guide](https://github.com/paoloronco/n8n-templates/blob/main/workflows/ai-instagram-publishing/README.md) · [Full documentation](https://paoloronco.notion.site/3f5f0ba27c32806ba425f7d84c72961a)\n\n",
        "height": 656,
        "width": 736
      },
      "id": "bf1ba0e6-6bf6-491f-8550-7cb4088d348a",
      "name": "NOTE 00 - Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1472,
        1632
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 01 · Collect RSS articles\n\nThe schedule reads the configured feed. Aggregate and Code nodes combine its articles into the structured input used by the selection agent.",
        "height": 352,
        "width": 672,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "48a4072e-a507-4c65-8066-a3ed0e524e96",
      "name": "NOTE 01 - Collect RSS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2304,
        1872
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 · Select relevant stories\n\nOpenAI picks up to three article IDs. Merge and Code nodes match those IDs to the original feed entries and pass their source URLs to the writer.",
        "height": 592,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "11434cc7-6ee3-4585-96f6-729a025c000d",
      "name": "NOTE 02 - Select stories",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2992,
        1632
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 03 · Write the post and image title\n\nThe writing agent creates the Instagram copy. Gmail emails the draft; a separate OpenAI step generates the image headline. The email does not pause publishing.",
        "height": 368,
        "width": 688,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "040d5216-f841-40fd-a5d3-8382896675fa",
      "name": "NOTE 03 - Write copy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3568,
        1856
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 04 · Generate and style the image\n\nOpenAI generates the visual. Image nodes apply the blur, headline and read-more text before the file is uploaded.",
        "height": 368,
        "width": 1104,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3d12affa-d7b1-47d8-86cd-f8af18c36391",
      "name": "NOTE 04 - Create image",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4304,
        1856
      ]
    },
    {
